   "unmapped": [
    "Complete cross-learning: playing an action reveals rewards of all out-neighbor actions under all M contexts",
    "Tabular contexts: M discrete contexts chosen by an oblivious adversary, no structure on mean rewards mu_{c,a}"
   ],
   "definition_quote": "At the beginning of each round $t\\in [T]$ during the time horizon $T$, an oblivious adversary chooses a context $c_t\\in [M]$ and reveals it to the learner, and the learner chooses an action $a_t\\in [K]$. There is a strongly observable directed feedback graph $G=([K],E)$ across the actions such that all rewards in $(r_{t,c,a})_{c\\in [M], (a_t, a)\\in E}$ are observable, where we assume no structure in the rewards except that $r_{t,c,a}\\in [0,1]$."
  },
